All tests pass.

**Root cause:** Newer llama-server reports prompt tokens served from the prompt cache in a separate `timings.cache_n` field, with `prompt_n` only counting freshly evaluated tokens. The Go structs `llamaServerCompletionResponse` and `llamaServerChatResponse` in `llm/llama_server.go` didn't decode `cache_n`, so `PromptEvalCount` was set to just `Timings.PromptN` — omitting cached tokens.

**Fix** (in `llm/llama_server.go`):
- Added `CacheN int \`json:"cache_n"\`` to both `Timings` structs.
- Changed the two `PromptEvalCount` assignments (completion stream at line ~1470 and chat stream at line ~1767) to `lsResp.Timings.CacheN + lsResp.Timings.PromptN`.

`go test -count=1 ./llm/...` → `ok github.com/ollama/ollama/llm`.
